                                                  Summer Internship Project Report
                                                         AI-Powered NLP
                                                        
->Introduction of the Project Undertaken
    Objective: Build AI-powered News Agent using LangChain, Groq API, and GNEWS API.
    Importance: Personalized and location-aware news delivery.
    Scope: Extensible to any NLP-based project (chatbots, assistants, RAG).
    Relevance: Combines real-world APIs with advanced AI models.

->Technologies Used
    LangChain – Orchestration of AI pipelines.
    Groq API – Fast LLM inference.
    Google Maps API – Accurate geolocation services.
    Streamlit – Interactive user interface.
    RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) – Enhanced responses with external data.
    Ollama – Access to pre-trained NLP models.

->Implementation Flow
    1. User opens the Streamlit App.
    2. Location is fetched using Google Maps API.
    3. Query sent to Groq LLM for news summarization.
    4. Localized results displayed in user-friendly UI.
    5. Supports extension with RAG and AI Agents.

->Conclusion
    Successfully built an AI-powered localized news agent.
    Learned integration of multiple APIs with AI models.
    Future Scope: Expand to multi-modal AI (text + voice + vision).
    Industry Relevance: Foundation for chatbots, assistants, and smart agents.

